# A core whose receiver is stuck mid-frame (QA4 NES stall shape: no
# core-ID replies, no pad frames) must come back by itself: after 1 s of
# silence with a game loaded the firmware flushes 2048 zero bytes, which
# complete the garbage frame, and the link answers again -- no restart,
# game still running, and the game menu works afterwards. Without the
# flush the fake stays stuck (polls alone need ~128 s to feed it 2048
# bytes) and the menu never opens.
expect-screen "TangCore"
press down
press down
press down
press down
press b
expect-screen "cgame.sms"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core smstang
wait 2s
rx-stuck on
wait 6s
# no restart happened and the game is still the running core
expect-core smstang
expect-overlay off
# the link answers again: pad frames flow and the menu opens
hold select+start+l 400ms
expect-screen "Close game"
expect-overlay on
